}
```
Reason:
The use of `hlist_for_each_entry()` to iterate over the list while freeing elements can lead to dereferencing a pointer to a freed memory location, causing a use-after-free vulnerability. When an element is freed, the iterator may still reference it, leading to undefined behavior.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
hlist_for_each_entry_safe(daemon, n, &ecryptfs_daemon_hash[i], euid_chain) {
    rc = ecryptfs_exorcise_daemon(daemon);
}
```
Reason:
The use of `hlist_for_each_entry_safe()` allows safe removal of elements during iteration by maintaining a reference to the next node in the list. This prevents dereferencing a pointer to a freed memory location, thus eliminating the use-after-free vulnerability.

